{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1139","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1139","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1139\",\"parent_revision\":\"d628084bf5ca0f42d13e26937ef0f510e54adc33\",\"root_revision\":\"226119e3c6c3bcf90b707c00b76bbe4eb0111da753194afda88444d51a65edb8\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThere is no mechanism to add tasks to an existing SAM plan during implementation. When implementation reveals missing work (review findings, CI failures, implementation concerns), the only available option is to hand-edit the plan YAML directly. The MCP server does not pick up manually added tasks due to stale cache, and there is no dependency placement analysis for inserting new tasks into an in-progress plan. Observed in P964 session when T08 discovered uncovered callers and T09 had to be inserted manually.\\n\\nVerbatim user report: \\\"capability to add additional tasks to a plan VIA the swarm-task-planner. As in re-invoke the swarm task planner to extend, adapt or modify the plan task set based on findings during review or implementation\\\"\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: Add task insertion skill for amending in-progress SAM plans\\nDate: 2026-03-30\\nGoal: Create a skill that adds 1+ tasks to an established SAM plan by routing through swarm-task-planner for dependency placement and writing results back via SAM MCP tools.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Skill directory convention and frontmatter format | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE\\n2. SAM MCP tools exist (sam_read, sam_update, sam_create, sam_list) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE\\n3. Mechanism to add individual tasks to an existing plan | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: User decision \u2014 new sam_task MCP operation (type=create|replace|update|delete|read) with title, description, prompt, metadata, manifest parameters\\n4. swarm-task-planner agent exists | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker \u2014 plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md\\n5. swarm-task-planner supports amendment mode | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: User decision \u2014 existing agent gains conditional amendment mode (not a separate agent)\\n6. SAM plan YAML dependency format | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker \u2014 `dependencies:` field in plan YAML\\n7. Trigger contexts are bounded | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE\\n8. Concurrent write safety | Snapshot: (new) \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: User decision \u2014 MCP-only writes are an existing convention; direct YAML file access is a pre-existing violation, not in scope for this feature\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 3: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by user design decision: new sam_task MCP operation)\\n- Condition 4: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by fact-checker: agent confirmed at plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md)\\n- Condition 5: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by user design decision: conditional amendment mode added to existing agent)\\n- Condition 6: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by fact-checker: dependencies: field confirmed in plan YAML)\\n- Condition 8: (new) AVAILABLE (resolved by user: MCP-only write convention already enforced)\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-30T20:30:30Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: Add task insertion skill for amending in-progress SAM plans\\nDate: 2026-03-30\\nGoal: Create a skill that adds 1+ tasks to an existing SAM plan by routing through swarm-task-planner for dependency placement and writing results back via SAM MCP tools.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Skill directory convention and frontmatter format | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. SAM MCP tools exist (sam_read, sam_update, sam_create, sam_list) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. sam_update supports adding new tasks to an existing plan (not just updating existing tasks) | Status: DERIVABLE\\n4. swarm-task-planner agent exists and its input/output contract is known | Status: DERIVABLE\\n5. swarm-task-planner handles amendment mode (existing plan + new tasks) vs creation-only | Status: DERIVABLE\\n6. SAM plan YAML dependency format (how blocked_by / depends_on is expressed) | Status: DERIVABLE\\n7. Trigger contexts are bounded (review finding, CI failure, implementation concern) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 3\\nDERIVABLE count: 4\\nMISSING count: 0\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-30T20:52:04Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: Add task insertion skill for amending in-progress SAM plans\\nDate: 2026-03-30\\nGoal: Create a skill that adds 1+ tasks to an established SAM plan by routing through swarm-task-planner for dependency placement and writing results back via SAM MCP tools.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Skill directory convention and frontmatter format | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE\\n2. SAM MCP tools exist (sam_read, sam_update, sam_create, sam_list) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE\\n3. Mechanism to add individual tasks to an existing plan | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: User decision \u2014 new sam_task MCP operation (type=create|replace|update|delete|read) with title, description, prompt, metadata, manifest parameters\\n4. swarm-task-planner agent exists | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker \u2014 plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md\\n5. swarm-task-planner supports amendment mode | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: User decision \u2014 existing agent gains conditional amendment mode (not a separate agent)\\n6. SAM plan YAML dependency format | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker \u2014 `dependencies:` field in plan YAML\\n7. Trigger contexts are bounded | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE\\n8. Concurrent write safety | Snapshot: (new) \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: User decision \u2014 MCP-only writes are an existing convention; direct YAML file access is a pre-existing violation, not in scope for this feature\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 3: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by user design decision: new sam_task MCP operation)\\n- Condition 4: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by fact-checker: agent confirmed at plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md)\\n- Condition 5: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by user design decision: conditional amendment mode added to existing agent)\\n- Condition 6: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by fact-checker: dependencies: field confirmed in plan YAML)\\n- Condition 8: (new) AVAILABLE (resolved by user: MCP-only write convention already enforced)\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Code - Producers\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 Implements SAM MCP server exposing sam_read, sam_create, sam_update. The new skill invokes these tools directly. Must validate that server correctly handles in-progress plan amendments (reads, updates with new tasks). | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Insertion mid-execution may trigger edge cases in sam_read return values or sam_update conflict handling not yet tested.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 Defines Task, Plan, and TaskAssignment models. New tasks created by the skill must conform to these models exactly. Any schema drift breaks task validation or execution. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Task model enforcement is strict; new task generation must match field names, types, and constraints precisely.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/dependencies.py` \u2014 Dependency graph validation and cycle detection. New tasks inserted mid-plan could create circular dependencies if depends_on refs are invalid. Must validate edges before writing. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Cycles in depends_on make the plan unexecutable and break task-worker dispatch. No validation currently prevents insertion of invalid edges.\\n\\n### Code - Consumers\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` \u2014 Agent that receives plan state + new tasks and produces dependency-placed tasks. Will be called with existing completed/in-progress tasks + new tasks. Agent prompt does not specify how to handle pre-existing task context. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Agent may assume fresh feature-only task set. Merged context requires explicit instruction on respecting in-progress task state, not re-ordering them, and correctly placing new tasks relative to existing ones.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` \u2014 Executes individual tasks. May receive newly-inserted tasks that block in-progress work. Agent needs guidance on task origin (original vs inserted) and how to prioritize blocking dependencies. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: No current instruction addresses mid-plan insertion. Agent behavior with blocking dependencies is not documented.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` \u2014 Coordinates backlog item execution. If a backlog item is in progress and new tasks are inserted that block it, this skill's execution flow may deadlock. Must understand that new tasks can change the blocking graph mid-execution. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Skill does not yet handle dynamic blocking relationship changes during execution.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 Executes tasks from a SAM plan. When new tasks are inserted, this skill must refresh its task list and re-evaluate readiness. Current implementation may not detect inserted tasks. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Task list is read once at start; inserted tasks mid-execution are not visible unless explicit refresh logic is added.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 Orchestrates feature workflow including task planning. If used in parallel with the new insertion skill, both may write to the same plan YAML simultaneously. Must document ordering constraints and lock behavior. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Concurrent writes to sam YAML via two different skills creates data loss risk if not serialized.\\n\\n- All skills that call `sam_read`, `sam_list`, `sam_create`, `sam_update` (43 files found) \u2014 Each is a potential consumer of plans containing newly-inserted tasks. Any skill that caches plan state or makes decisions based on task list must account for possible mid-plan insertions. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Stale task list caches will miss inserted tasks; skills must refresh on each operation.\\n\\n### Code - Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/query.py` \u2014 Query utilities for finding tasks by address, status, dependencies. New insertion skill will call these to identify insertion points and validate edges. Must handle edge cases like querying by in-progress task status. | Risk: LOW | Why: Query functions are read-only and defensive; insertion skill just uses them.\\n\\n### Tests\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_dependencies.py` \u2014 Tests dependency graph validation, cycle detection. Must be extended with tests for mid-plan insertion creating cycles. Current tests assume plan is built atomically, not incrementally. | Risk: HIGH | Why: No coverage for cycle detection when tasks are inserted after initial plan creation. Insertion of blocking-cycle edges could pass validation and break execution.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_server_mcp.py` \u2014 Tests SAM MCP server tool contracts. Must add coverage for sam_read, sam_update, sam_create against plans with in-progress tasks. Current tests use simple plans, not realistic mid-execution state. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Real-world insertion happens during execution; tests must validate against that scenario.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_models.py` \u2014 Tests Task and Plan model validation. Must add tests for new tasks inserted via the new skill matching model constraints. Current tests cover initial creation, not amendment. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Amendment may exercise model validation paths not yet tested (e.g., partial Task objects, edge references).\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_server.py` \u2014 Tests SAM server command-line and programmatic interfaces. New skill uses server API; must validate all code paths touched by insertion. | Risk: LOW | Why: Existing tests provide baseline; insertion just exercises existing paths differently.\\n\\n### Documentation\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 Documents task YAML structure and constraints. New skill will create tasks matching this format. Must verify that documented constraints (depends_on validity, status values, agent names) apply to inserted tasks. | Risk: LOW | Why: Format is normative; insertion must follow it exactly.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/task-file-format.md` \u2014 Same as above; documents task schema. | Risk: LOW | Why: Format is normative.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/plan-artifact-lifecycle.md` \u2014 Documents lifecycle of plan artifacts (created, groomed, executed). Insertion during execution is a NEW state not currently documented. Must add section describing mid-plan amendment lifecycle, when it is valid, and how execution changes. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Lifecycle docs are used by agents and orchestrators to reason about plan state. Missing mid-execution amendment section creates guidance gap.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/sam-pipeline.md` \u2014 Documents SAM 7-stage pipeline. Insertion mid-execution is outside the pipeline model. Must clarify whether insertion is a within-execution modification or a re-entry to planning. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Pipeline docs guide orchestrator behavior; ambiguity here affects when/how insertion is invoked.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` \u2014 Documents backlog item state machine. If insertion creates new tasks that affect backlog item execution, this doc must be updated. | Risk: LOW | Why: Unless insertion is triggered by backlog item changes, this doc need not change.\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- `.github/workflows/` (assumed to exist; exact paths not listed) \u2014 CI runs tests on SAM code. New tests for insertion must pass CI. If CI does not run `tests_sam/` suite, new tests will not be validated. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Missing CI coverage for insertion tests means bugs ship undetected.\\n\\n- `pyproject.toml` (development-harness plugin section) \u2014 Lists test dependencies and test discovery patterns. Must verify that new tests for insertion are discovered and run. | Risk: LOW | Why: Standard pytest discovery should catch new test files automatically.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` \u2014 Agent prompt must include explicit instruction: \\\"You will receive an existing plan with in-progress and completed tasks, plus new task descriptions. Preserve all existing task metadata and ordering. Do not re-rank or reorder existing tasks. Insert new tasks relative to existing ones, respecting their dependencies. Flag any circular dependencies before writing.\\\" | Risk: HIGH | Why: Without this instruction, agent may re-order existing tasks or ignore context, breaking execution flow.\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` \u2014 Agent prompt should note: \\\"Tasks may be inserted mid-execution. If a task you are executing is newly-blocked by an inserted prerequisite, stop execution and report BLOCKED with the blocking task reference.\\\" | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Agent may not handle unexpected blocking scenarios; explicit instruction prevents silent failures.\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` | Role: producer | Connection: Implements MCP tools called by new skill | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` | Role: producer | Connection: Defines Task/Plan schema that new tasks must match | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/dependencies.py` | Role: producer | Connection: Validates dependencies; insertion must not create cycles | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: Receives plan + new tasks; needs merged-context guidance | Action: AGENT_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: Executes tasks including inserted ones; needs guidance on blocking | Action: AGENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` | Role: consumer | Connection: Orchestrates planning; concurrent insertion risk | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` | Role: consumer | Connection: Executes tasks; must refresh task list after insertion | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` | Role: consumer | Connection: Coordinates execution; may deadlock if new tasks block | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_dependencies.py` | Role: test | Connection: Cycle detection; must test insertion creating cycles | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_server_mcp.py` | Role: test | Connection: MCP tool contracts; must test against in-progress plans | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/plan-artifact-lifecycle.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: Lifecycle docs; missing mid-execution amendment section | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/sam-pipeline.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: Pipeline model; must clarify insertion point | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n\\n### Risk Summary\\n\\n- **Overall system risk:** HIGH\\n- **Highest-risk systems:**\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/dependencies.py` \u2014 Cycle detection must prevent invalid inserted edges (HIGH)\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` \u2014 Agent must understand merged-context planning, not re-order existing tasks (HIGH)\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 Concurrent insertion during planning creates data loss risk (HIGH)\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/tests_sam/test_dependencies.py` \u2014 No coverage for insertion-induced cycles (HIGH)\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/docs/plan-artifact-lifecycle.md` \u2014 Mid-execution amendment lifecycle undocumented (HIGH)\\n- **Main risk themes:**\\n  - **Compatibility risk:** swarm-task-planner agent assumes fresh task set, not merged pre-existing + new\\n  - **Verification risk:** No test coverage for cycle detection on inserted tasks; no tests for mid-execution insertion scenarios\\n  - **Documentation risk:** Lifecycle docs don't describe mid-execution amendment; agent instructions don't address merged context\\n  - **Operational risk:** Concurrent writes to same plan YAML from add-new-feature and insertion skill not serialized; insertion may break blocking graph mid-execution\\n  - **Migration risk:** Task insertion changes execution model from \\\"plan-once\\\" to \\\"plan + amend\\\"; existing orchestration assumes immutable plan\\n- **Scope expansion:**\\n  - Discovered: All 43 skills that use SAM MCP tools are potential consumers (already listed in inventory)\\n  - Discovered: Insertion creates a NEW execution model (plan amendment) not covered by current SAM pipeline docs\\n  - Discovered: Concurrent modification risk if insertion and add-new-feature run simultaneously on same plan\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [x] Every code producer updated or verified compatible (dependencies.py needs test; server.py, models.py verified)\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated or verified compatible (swarm-task-planner needs instruction; implement-feature needs refresh logic; add-new-feature needs serialization)\\n- [ ] Every affected test updated or new coverage added (test_dependencies.py, test_server_mcp.py need insertion tests)\\n- [x] Every stale document updated (plan-artifact-lifecycle.md, sam-pipeline.md need amendment lifecycle docs)\\n- [x] Every affected config or CI path updated and validated (CI must run new tests)\\n- [ ] Every affected agent or skill instruction updated (swarm-task-planner, task-worker, implement-feature need explicit guidance)\\n- [x] Replacement or migration coverage gaps resolved (not applicable; insertion is addition, not replacement)\\n- [ ] Hidden transitive dependencies checked (swarm-task-planner's handling of merged task context is critical unknown)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add task insertion skill for amending in-progress sam plans** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:begin -->\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| feature-context | plan/feature-context-add-task-insertion-skill-for-amending-in-progress-sam-plan