ndency placement analysis. This blocks efficient plan management during implementation and forces unsafe out-of-band edits every time implementation reveals missing work.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-30T20:55:43Z-1</sub>\\n\\nWhen this ships:\\n- Mid-execution task insertion becomes a single skill invocation \u2014 no YAML editing\\n- swarm-task-planner performs dependency analysis against the existing plan, placing new tasks in the correct position including as prerequisites of in-progress tasks\\n- Inserted tasks are written via MCP tools, making them immediately visible to all SAM consumers\\n- Review findings, CI failures, and implementation concerns produce trackable tasks rather than ad-hoc interruptions\\n- The sam_task MCP operation provides a clean, typed API for programmatic plan amendment reusable by other agents and skills\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-30T20:55:43Z-2</sub>\\n\\nUser invokes the skill with: a SAM plan reference, one or more task descriptions, and a trigger context (review finding / CI failure / implementation concern).\\n\\nThe skill:\\n1. Reads the current plan state (all tasks, statuses, dependencies) via SAM MCP tools\\n2. Passes plan state + new task descriptions to swarm-task-planner in amendment mode\\n3. swarm-task-planner returns: amended task set with new tasks placed at correct dependency positions, including `dependencies:` fields and blocking relationships for in-progress tasks\\n4. Writes each new task to the plan via the `sam_task` MCP operation (type=create)\\n5. Prints a report:\\n   - Tasks added: title, generated ID\\n   - What each blocks: IDs of in-progress or pending tasks that now depend on each new task\\n   - What each depends on: IDs of tasks each new task requires before it can start\\n\\nThe trigger context is passed through to swarm-task-planner to inform priority and placement reasoning. The skill does not modify or reorder existing tasks \u2014 it inserts only.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-30T20:55:43