()` is the only tool that creates new tasks.  \\nImplication: Task insertion requires new mechanism (new MCP operation, extension to sam_update, or read-modify-write pattern).\\n\\n**Claim 2: swarm-task-planner agent exists**  \\nVerdict: **VERIFIED**  \\nEvidence: File found at plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md  \\nStatus: Agent is available but scope is limited (creation-only, no amendment mode).\\n\\n**Claim 3: swarm-task-planner handles amendment mode**  \\nVerdict: **REFUTED**  \\nEvidence: Agent frontmatter includes only `sam_create` tool (not `sam_update`). Prompt documentation (lines 260-290) shows exclusive use of `sam_create` for plan generation. No amendment workflows documented. Agent lacks access to `sam_update` for modifying existing plans.  \\nImplication: Agent scope must be extended to support merged-context planning (existing tasks + new tasks).\\n\\n**Claim 4: SAM plan YAML uses dependency format (blocked_by, depends_on, or similar)**  \\nVerdict: **VERIFIED**  \\nEvidence: Real SAM plans use `dependencies:` field (list of task IDs per task).  \\nFormat validated against: Test fixtures at tests_sam/fixtures/ showing consistent structure.  \\nStatus: Dependency format is stable and documented.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Highest-Risk Areas\\n\\n**1. Concurrent write safety (CRITICAL)**  \\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` may write to plan YAML simultaneously with new insertion skill\\n- Risk: Data corruption, lost tasks, merge conflicts\\n- Action: Add file locking or versioning to SAM MCP\\n\\n**2. Agent context merging (CRITICAL)**  \\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` assumes fresh task set, not pre-existing + new\\n- Risk: Agent may re-rank existing tasks, break execution ordering, violate in-progress task constraints\\n- Action: Add explicit merged-context instructions to agent prompt\\n\\n**3. Cycle detection (CRITICAL)**  \\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/dependencies.py` has no test coverage for insertion creating circular dependencies\\n- Risk: Inserted task with invalid `depends_on` edge silently passes validation, breaks task execution\\n- Action: Add tests for cycle detection on mid-plan insertion\\n\\n**4. Documentation gaps (HIGH)**  \\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/plan-artifact-lifecycle.md` missing mid-execution amendment section\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/sdlc-layers/layer-0/sam-pipeline.md` doesn't clarify insertion point in 7-stage pipeline\\n- Risk: Agents and orchestrators lack guidance on when/how insertion is valid\\n- Action: Document mid-execution amendment lifecycle\\n\\n**5. Task list refresh (MEDIUM)**  \\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` reads task list once at start; inserted tasks are not visible\\n- Risk: Newly-inserted blocking tasks don't prevent downstream work from starting\\n- Action: Add explicit refresh logic after task insertion\\n\\n### Overview\\n\\nFour factual claims about SAM MCP capabilities and swarm-task-planner behavior were assessed. Two were verified; two were refuted. Refuted claims describe the implementation scope (missing features).\\n\\n### Risk Themes\\n\\n**Compatibility Risk**  \\nswarm-task-planner agent assumes fresh feature-only task set, not merged pre-existing + new. Without explicit instruction, agent will re-optimize task ordering and dependencies, breaking execution flow for in-progress tasks.\\n\\n**Verification Risk**  \\nZero test coverage for insertion creating cycles or for mid-execution insertion scenarios. Cycle detection may pass invalid edges; inserted tasks may trigger previously-untested code paths in task execution.\\n\\n**Documentation Risk**  \\nLifecycle and pipeline docs describe plan creation only, not mid-execution amendment. Agents and orchestrators lack guidance on when insertion is valid and how it affects execution state.\\n\\n**Operational Risk**  \\nConcurrent writes to same plan YAML from add-new-feature and insertion skill are not serialized. Simultaneous modifications corrupt plan state or lose tasks.\\n\\n**Migration Risk**  \\nInsertion changes execution model from \\\"plan-once\\\" to \\\"plan + amend\\\". Existing orchestration assumes immutable plan state; new insertion model breaks that assumption without explicit handling.\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:begin -->\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| feature-context | plan/feature-context-add-task-insertion-skill-for-amending-in-progress-sam-plans.md | current | discovery | 2026-03-30T20:29:42.164225+00:00 |\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:end -->\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"b5b07ab835f46d7e4f9261e3dc76647e4c69c1ba666686ac2040a134b782e058\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPtZ6XA\"}"}